-- flight_log.rofl — CRAM §5: the question that shuts both doors.
--
-- Loaded on top of cram.rofl when the ground wants the craft to be able to
-- account for itself FROM THE INSIDE — not "what did you conclude" (the craft
-- always knows that) but "which rule concluded it, and on which tick".
--
-- These four rules read `derived_by` in a body, and that single syntactic fact
-- is read by `Evaluation.readsProvenance`, which two policies consult:
--
--   RETENTION refuses. `Rofl.frozenRetention` returns undefined for such a
--   program whatever `retainTicks` says, because pruning would no longer evict
--   a cache — it would change a derivable fact. `quiet[log](T)` below is that
--   fact, and it is the sharp case: pruned, it does not go missing, it goes
--   TRUE. The store would start asserting that the computer sat idle through
--   ticks it in fact worked through. demo.ts §8 performs exactly that sweep by
--   hand, on a copy, to show what the refusal is protecting.
--
--   REUSE refuses, for its own reason: every firing anywhere in the program
--   emits a provenance record, so a rule reading provenance is triggered by
--   derivations everywhere and sits outside the dependency cone that reuse's
--   fingerprint argument rests on.
--
-- One predicate, two policies, and they cannot come to different conclusions
-- about the same program. Measured in demo.ts §7: loading this file makes the
-- run cost 9.5x the firings and takes the store off any bound at all.

-- Which rule fired on which tick. The join is trivial and the reach is not:
-- this is the whole provenance table, and it is the table the policy exists
-- to bound.
fired_at[log](R, T)   :- derived_by(_, R, T).

-- A tick the computer did work in.
active[log](T)        :- fired_at[log](_, T).

-- THE FACT THAT WOULD MOVE. A tick that happened and in which nothing at all
-- was concluded — a stalled computer, which for a probe is the failure worth
-- catching. `tick_no[log]` is published by the ground: it is the ground's
-- record of which ticks the craft is believed to have lived through, and it is
-- deliberately NOT derived from the provenance, or the question would answer
-- itself.
quiet[log](T)         :- tick_no[log](T), not active[log](T).

tick_no[log](T)       @next :- tick_no[log](T).
